  "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Crompton Instruments (TE) INTEGRA 1540/1560/1580 digital metering systems on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Crompton INTEGRA 15xx: 97 objects (64 AI, 33 AO), 43 polled by default. Inputs give phase voltages and currents, W, VA, VAR, PF and angle per phase, averages and sums, frequency, import/export Wh and varh, demand and max demand. Unpolled outputs hold the meter setup (demand period, system type, CT/PT, pulse, password, analog outputs).",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Crompton_INTEGRA_15XXX_Meter_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Integra15xx.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 43 of the 97 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Volts 1 is missing from the profile as published; the first object is Volts 2."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Crompton_INTEGRA_15XXX_Meter_a",
    "doc_number": "Crompton_INTEGRA_15XXX_Meter_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Crompton_INTEGRA_15XX_Meter.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Map total active power (W sum), imported energy (Wh) and average voltage first. The listed objects are read-only.",
